          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The water shortage and fallen shade cloth are resolved, though the final brown leaf weakens the sense of closure.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia shares the limited water and shelters both plants, but the promised repair and static final image leave the problem only partly resolved.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia shares water and moves both plants under the umbrella; the story ends before the tap is fixed or the fallen shade cloth restored.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The tap and shade cloth are repaired after Nia waters the sunflower first, but the lingering brown leaf makes the ending feel unresolved.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"Nia waters the seedlings first, then uses the repaired tap for the sunflower; both plants end together beside the restored shade cloth.\",\"group_id\":2},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The equal-sharing and sheltering actions are clear, but the promised repair is deferred and the ending offers little change beyond placement.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000053\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia distributes scarce water and shelters both plants, but the tap and fallen shade cloth remain unresolved at the close.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The plants receive water and the shade cloth is repaired, although the seedlings retain a brown leaf in the final image.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The tap and cloth are repaired after the sunflower is watered first, but the repeated brown-leaf detail leaves a small problem hanging.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000048\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"Nia waters the seedlings first and then the sunflower, ending with both plants together beneath repaired shade.\",\"group_id\":2}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":1,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share the same garden dilemma: a broken tap, one can of rainwater, thirsty plants, and fallen shade cloth. Stories s000014, s000023, s000021, and s000034 follow the sunflower-first path, with a brown leaf remaining; s000028, s000058, s000017, and s000053 share the water-and-shelter path with repair deferred; s000036 and s000048 water seedlings first, then the sunflower after the tap is fixed. These are limited branch variations rather than distinct premises or outcomes.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Nia waters the sunflower first from scarce stored water; seedlings show a brown leaf, then the tap and shade cloth are repaired, leaving that damage visible.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"Nia divides the stored water between both plants and shelters them under an umbrella; the tap repair is promised for later and the fallen shade cloth remains unrestored.\"},{\"group_id\":2,\"summary\":\"Nia waters the seedlings first, then uses the repaired tap to water the sunflower; the shade cloth is restored and both plants are placed together.\"}]}",
